{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-day-kids-spain/audio/main-f3b53c2c0f54.mp3","durationSec":271.368,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.15,"text":"The day starts with breakfast."},{"start":1.14,"end":4.02,"text":"Breakfast in Spain is small."},{"start":4.58,"end":6.56,"text":"Many children eat toast and drink juice."},{"start":7.46,"end":8.94,"text":"Some children drink Colacao."},{"start":9.76,"end":11.64,"text":"Colacao is a chocolate milk drink."},{"start":12.9,"end":14.82,"text":"School starts at nine o'clock."},{"start":14.82,"end":16.46,"text":"In the morning, children have a break."},{"start":16.96,"end":18.6,"text":"They eat a snack, a little food."},{"start":19.48,"end":21.83,"text":"Many children bring fruit or a bocadillo."},{"start":21.83,"end":23.66,"text":"A bocadillo is a big sandwich."},{"start":24.2,"end":26.16,"text":"It often has ham or cheese inside."},{"start":27.08,"end":28.08,"text":"Why do they eat at school?"},{"start":28.66,"end":31.48,"text":"Lunch in Spain is late, so children get hungry!"},{"start":31.48,"end":35.04,"text":"Many children finish school at two o'clock."},{"start":35.04,"end":36.04,"text":"They go home for lunch."},{"start":36.96,"end":38.4,"text":"Other children eat lunch at school."},{"start":38.94,"end":40.02,"text":"Then they have more classes."},{"start":40.8,"end":42.64,"text":"They go home at half past four."},{"start":43.52,"end":45.48,"text":"Lunch is at about two o'clock."},{"start":45.48,"end":47.04,"text":"It is the biggest meal of the day."},{"start":47.74,"end":49.74,"text":"Children eat meat, fish or rice."},{"start":50.3,"end":51.02,"text":"Then they eat dessert."},{"start":51.02,"end":52.62,"text":"Lunch time is long."},{"start":53.16,"end":54.7,"text":"It can be two or three hours!"},{"start":55.66,"end":57.28,"text":"Lunch is the big family meal."},{"start":57.28,"end":59.68,"text":"At five o'clock, children are hungry again."},{"start":60.44,"end":61.99,"text":"Now it is time for merienda."},{"start":61.99,"end":64.04,"text":"Merienda is the afternoon snack."},{"start":64.72,"end":66.2,"text":"Children eat a bocadillo with meat."},{"start":66.6,"end":67.78,"text":"Or they have milk and cookies."},{"start":68.36,"end":69.1,"text":"Why another snack?"},{"start":69.88,"end":71.46,"text":"Dinner in Spain is very late."},{"start":72.1,"end":74.18,"text":"After merienda, children go to the plaza."},{"start":74.94,"end":77.1,"text":"A plaza is a big open place in a town."},{"start":77.82,"end":79.32,"text":"Many plazas have a playground."},{"start":80.02,"end":81.26,"text":"Children run and play there."},{"start":81.26,"end":83.1,"text":"Parents sit and talk with friends."},{"start":83.36,"end":84.7,"text":"They watch all the children together."},{"start":85.64,"end":88.22,"text":"In summer, the day in Spain is very hot."},{"start":88.66,"end":89.56,"text":"The evening is cool."},{"start":89.9,"end":91.92,"text":"So children play outside until late."},{"start":93.3,"end":93.77,"text":"Spain loves basketball."},{"start":93.76,"end":96.86,"text":"Basketball clubs are all over Spain."},{"start":96.86,"end":99.68,"text":"Children from 8 to 14 learn with a coach."},{"start":100.4,"end":101.94,"text":"A coach is a basketball teacher."},{"start":102.48,"end":104.58,"text":"They learn to run with the ball and throw it."},{"start":105.8,"end":107.72,"text":"Small children play minibasket."},{"start":107.72,"end":110.1,"text":"In minibasket, the basket is not so high."},{"start":110.3,"end":112.18,"text":"So small children can get the ball in."},{"start":112.54,"end":113.94,"text":"Why do so many kids play?"},{"start":114.92,"end":117.56,"text":"Spain was number one in the world in 2006."},{"start":117.56,"end":120.66,"text":"It was number one again in 2019."},{"start":121.54,"end":122.62,"text":"Children watched the team win."},{"start":123.08,"end":124.78,"text":"Then many children wanted to play too."},{"start":125.74,"end":128.2,"text":"One big star is Pau Gasol from Barcelona."},{"start":129,"end":130.8,"text":"He is 2.13 meters tall!"},{"start":131.86,"end":133.68,"text":"Dinner is at about nine o'clock."},{"start":133.68,"end":135.56,"text":"Some families eat at ten!"},{"start":135.56,"end":137.6,"text":"Dinner is small, because lunch was big."},{"start":138.98,"end":140.26,"text":"Children often eat tortilla."},{"start":141.05,"end":144.26,"text":"In Spain, a tortilla is made with eggs and potatoes."},{"start":144.86,"end":146.28,"text":"It is thick, like a cake."},{"start":146.28,"end":149.08,"text":"After dinner, children go to bed."},{"start":149.84,"end":150.4,"text":"It is late!"},{"start":151.2,"end":152.56,"text":"But school starts at nine."},{"start":152.98,"end":154.7,"text":"So the morning is not very early."},{"start":155.92,"end":159.28,"text":"Children in Spain get big presents on January 6."},{"start":159.28,"end":159.92,"text":"Who brings them?"},{"start":160.66,"end":161.44,"text":"The Three Kings!"},{"start":162.34,"end":164.68,"text":"In an old story, three kings come on camels."},{"start":165.22,"end":166.88,"text":"They bring presents to baby Jesus."},{"start":167.42,"end":171.02,"text":"On the evening of January 5, big towns have a parade."},{"start":171.02,"end":173.76,"text":"A parade is a long line of people in the street."},{"start":174.3,"end":176.04,"text":"There is music, and there are big cars."},{"start":176.04,"end":178.92,"text":"The kings are in the parade, and they throw candy."},{"start":179.68,"end":180.94,"text":"Many children bring an umbrella."},{"start":181.4,"end":181.62,"text":"Why?"},{"start":182.1,"end":184.08,"text":"They open it and hold it with the top down."},{"start":184.74,"end":186,"text":"Now it is like a big cup."},{"start":186.44,"end":187.92,"text":"They can catch lots of candy!"},{"start":189.3,"end":191.38,"text":"At night, children put their shoes by the door."},{"start":191.78,"end":193.52,"text":"The kings leave presents there."},{"start":194.2,"end":195.94,"text":"Children leave a drink for each king."},{"start":196.42,"end":198.62,"text":"They leave food and water for the animals too."},{"start":199.2,"end":201.6,"text":"The animals walk a long way, so they are hungry!"},{"start":202.72,"end":204.58,"text":"In the morning, children find their presents."},{"start":204.58,"end":207.1,"text":"Families eat roscón."},{"start":207.1,"end":209.62,"text":"Roscón is a big cake with a hole in it."},{"start":209.92,"end":211.14,"text":"A little toy is inside."},{"start":211.74,"end":214.42,"text":"Find the toy, and you are king or queen for the day!"},{"start":214.94,"end":218,"text":"Find a bean, and you buy the cake one year later."},{"start":219.02,"end":222.1,"text":"On your birthday in Spain, your family pulls your ears!"},{"start":222.64,"end":224.18,"text":"They do it one time for every year."},{"start":224.72,"end":225.28,"text":"Are you seven?"},{"start":225.28,"end":226.62,"text":"Then you get seven!"},{"start":226.62,"end":228.12,"text":"Why?"},{"start":228.12,"end":230.64,"text":"People say ears grow all your life."},{"start":231.26,"end":233.2,"text":"So it means: have a long life!"},{"start":235.44,"end":238.88,"text":"When a tooth comes out, children in Spain wait for a mouse."},{"start":239.58,"end":242.52,"text":"His name is Ratoncito Pérez."},{"start":242.52,"end":244.58,"text":"The child puts the tooth under the pillow."},{"start":245.06,"end":247.12,"text":"At night, the mouse takes the tooth."},{"start":247.76,"end":250.8,"text":"He leaves a little money, candy or a small present."},{"start":251.88,"end":252.52,"text":"Why a mouse?"},{"start":253.14,"end":256.08,"text":"A long time ago, a boy king lived in Spain."},{"start":256.76,"end":257.7,"text":"His tooth came out."},{"start":258.1,"end":259.08,"text":"He was eight years old."},{"start":259.68,"end":261.54,"text":"His mother asked a writer for a story."},{"start":262.3,"end":264.38,"text":"The writer made a story about a little mouse."},{"start":265.26,"end":268.2,"text":"In the story, the mouse lives in a box of cookies."},{"start":269.02,"end":270.78,"text":"The box is in a house in Madrid."}],"words":[{"text":"The","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"day","start":0.16,"end":0.38},{"text":"starts","start":0.38,"end":0.78},{"text":"with","start":0.78,"end":1.14},{"text":"breakfast","start":1.14,"end":1.15},{"text":"Breakfast","start":1.14,"end":1.6},{"text":"in","start":2.9,"end":3.12},{"text":"Spain","start":3.12,"end":3.42},{"text":"is","start":3.42,"end":3.64},{"text":"small","start":3.64,"end":4.02},{"text":"Many","start":4.58,"end":4.7},{"text":"children","start":4.7,"end":5},{"text":"eat","start":5,"end":5.26},{"text":"toast","start":5.26,"end":5.62},{"text":"and","start":5.62,"end":6},{"text":"drink","start":6,"end":6.22},{"text":"juice","start":6.22,"end":6.56},{"text":"Some","start":7.46,"end":7.64},{"text":"children","start":7.64,"end":7.98},{"text":"drink","start":7.98,"end":8.32},{"text":"Colacao","start":8.32,"end":8.94},{"text":"Colacao","start":9.76,"end":10.26},{"text":"is","start":10.26,"end":10.48},{"text":"a","start":10.48,"end":10.62},{"text":"chocolate","start":10.62,"end":10.94},{"text":"milk","start":10.94,"end":11.26},{"text":"drink","start":11.26,"end":11.64},{"text":"School","start":12.9,"end":13},{"text":"starts","start":13,"end":13.34},{"text":"at","start":13.34,"end":13.52},{"text":"nine","start":13.52,"end":13.7},{"text":"o'clock","start":13.7,"end":14.82},{"text":"In","start":14.82,"end":14.94},{"text":"the","start":14.94,"end":15.06},{"text":"morning","start":15.06,"end":15.36},{"text":"children","start":15.54,"end":15.74},{"text":"have","start":15.74,"end":16.04},{"text":"a","start":16.04,"end":16.2},{"text":"break","start":16.2,"end":16.46},{"text":"They","start":16.96,"end":17.1},{"text":"eat","start":17.1,"end":17.2},{"text":"a","start":17.2,"end":17.34},{"text":"snack","start":17.34,"end":17.68},{"text":"a","start":17.98,"end":18.1},{"text":"little","start":18